  "parent_review_method": "The parent read the 22 current callsite contexts around manifest/config construction, cwd, env and argv, independently read the shared helper and floor indirection, and rechecked their exact source identities. The raw delegate reports are bounded discovery/context corroboration; their excerpts alone do not prove that review or an exhaustive dynamic launch census.",
  "semantic_facts": [
    {
      "id": "finite-owned-invocations",
      "facts": [
        "The 22 installation/local-pack routes were read with their manifest, cwd, environment and npmToolingOptions calls. The historical 21 remain, with one separately enumerated dialog-focus-reinsert caller.",
        "The new caller copies the explicit local library tarball into its owned temp consumer, generates dependencies using browserConsumerDependencies from the validated supported library line and pinned peer inputs, writes install-links/fund/audit project configuration, and invokes the literal install --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund --package-lock array through npmToolingOptions.",
        "Fixture TypeScript, compiler/linker/esbuild and Chrome execution follows installation. Those programs remain executable dependencies; their code is not being certified by the npm source identity profile.",
        "The current caller roster must bind the historical roster plus exactly this additional path. It is now a separate explicit input, without rewriting the historical roster."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "shared-owner-and-project-inputs",
      "facts": [
        "npm-tooling-options.mjs is byte-identical to the accepted e041 source. It validates absolute existing directory cwd and a finite argv vocabulary. Install/ci flags are limited; pack requires a local path and explicit absolute destination; version queries accept no extra args.",
        "It copies env, removes case-insensitive npm_* and the specified auth token names, sets private owned cache and blank user/global config, fixed registry/global/workspaces/ignore_scripts/online/cache/notifier settings, and preserves other environment. Project npmrc/package/lock inputs still matter.",
        "Root .npmrc, toolchain-lock.json, chainman.toml and justfile are unchanged from e041. No general assertion about arbitrary inherited PATH/NODE_OPTIONS/peer/compiler overrides follows."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "version-and-config-routes",
      "facts": [
        "The five separately identified version routes are the writer, pack checker, RC prepack observer, toolchain runtime checker and floor npm CLI resolver. The first four retain inherited env and cannot receive npmToolingOptions isolation credit. Floor resolution uses fixed command -v npm, realpath suffix validation and pinned version before passing the selected CLI.",
        "The optional tests/npm_tooling_options_probe.mjs route takes NGX_NPM_PROFILE_CLI from a trusted operator and invokes exact --version and config list --json arrays. It is unchanged from e041.",
        "The root executed this actual configuration probe with Node24.21.0 and npm11.19.0, authenticated every extracted regular CLI file against the pinned npm archive, and observed 17 rejected commands plus expected configuration. npm loads configuration before its version return; separate inherited-env version callers retain that boundary."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "floor-runtime-context",
      "facts": [
        "consumer-floor-plan.json moved from input to support because literal traversal now reaches it; its bytes changed. This remains live acquisition/selection configuration, with exact platform-specific linux-x64/linux-arm64 runtime URL and hash pins, rather than inert report data.",
        "The floor runtime owner verifies the selected URL shape/platform, downloaded archive size/hash, member paths, executable version and platform. It supplies selected Node and the resolved npm CLI to packed-consumer. The packed-consumer wrapper retains the same helper-guarded install argv and records the observed platform.",
        "This context review does not grant floor execution qualification, prove external release age, or renew any old brace-input validation. Five of the six historical brace inputs retain bytes; the changed floor plan requires distinct current-source boundary review before any successor advisory disposition."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "source-dispatch-and-executable-helpers",
      "facts": [
        "Changed CI/RC paths select finite source lifecycle tests and the nine-case typeahead runner. Typeahead launches fixed staged build and Karma commands, not a new npm operation. Browser coordinated acceptance and the ordinary scenario table are separate dispatch paths; their existing installation producers remain in the 22-row roster.",
        "Current source qualification readers use historical Git images as comparison DATA while running physically authenticated current helper programs. compile/exec/Function current loaders are actual execution and are not described as inert metadata.",
        "New Sass isolated expected computation executes a verified builtin bootstrap and finite manifest-selected snapshot entries. The code supplies reduced environment and Node permission arguments. Sass/immutable/peer implementation internals are outside this finite npm-command review.",
        "The two new scoped fixture runners permit externally selected compiler/peer/helper roots. Those remain within the historical trusted compiler/operator override exclusion; they are not arbitrary maintained npm command admissions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "discovery-and-bounds",
      "facts": [
        "The full primary source and recursive test/support populations remain exact physical SHA/size/Git-blob bindings; hashes do not stand in for the contextual facts above. The sole trusted source exclusion remains the checker itself.",
        "The provisional V4 census omitted the new current-caller roster from its input set. Root caught this against the maintained caller probe before profile issuance; V6 adds that exact finite input. Earlier provisional census digests in raw review records are historical discovery DATA. The marker binds the fresh V6 projection.",
        "The one generated dist FESM reference remains excluded from first-party committed source admission by exact ignored-generated handling. Packed/generated artifact bytes require their own qualification. No broad filename waiver or historical execution permission is created."
      ]
    }
  ],
